   224	## 3. Lemma W (the forced residue becomes spread)
   225	
   226	**Cited.**
   227	- **(BT)** Montgomery–Vaughan, "The large sieve", Mathematika 20 (1973) 119–134, Theorem 2:
   228	  π(x + y; q, a) − π(x; q, a) < 2y/(φ(q) log(y/q)) for q < y. We use the specialization
   229	  π(x; q, a) ≤ 2x/(φ(q) log(x/q)).
   230	- **(PNT)** π(2W) − π(W) ≥ W/(2 log W) for W ≥ W₀.
   231	
   232	**Lemma W [proved].** For all N ≥ N₀(d, k, μ, σ, η₀), every t ∈ [1, 2MV_max] and every a ∈ Z,
   233	  Pr_w[w ≡ a (mod t)] ≤ C_W/φ(t),  with C_W := 24/η₀.
   234	*Proof.*
   235	- If (a, t) > 1 the probability is 0.
   236	- Otherwise the count is ≤ π(2W; t, a) ≤ 4W/(φ(t) log(2W/t)). Divide by W/(2 log W).
   237	- log W ≤ log N, and log(2W/t) ≥ (η₀/2) log N − O(Λ) ≥ (η₀/3) log N. ∎
   238	- The interval form of BT would give about 12/η₀ (literature critic).
   239	- Choosing W/(2MV_max) and H/W to be suitable fixed powers of L, instead of N^{η₀/2}, would make the slack
   240	  o(1) at a polylogarithmic cost in C_W (codex). This changes no exponent.

