   446	## 6. Theorem A‴
   447	
   448	**Theorem A‴ [conditional].**
   449	- **Hypotheses.** Fix odd d ≥ 3, k > (d+1)/4, μ ∈ [ν + η₀, 1) and η₀ > 0. Let h := h_*(μ) + η₀, and assume
   450	  θ := 2μ + h + (d−1)ν ≤ 1. Put a := θ/√2 and B = L[1/2, a]. Assume:
   451	  - **LV6** for the law 𝒜‴, and for the field-selected law derived from it. This means LV §6 adapted to:
   452	    pure-descent rows at height V; the non-monic pair (f, g₁x − g₀) with Res = ±Nw; a leading coefficient
   453	    a_d ≡ Nw g₀^{−d} (mod g₁) that depends on w; possibly a restriction to unit leading coefficients mod N
   454	    (codex blind §4 shows this costs only a logarithm in FM); the content of f (it divides Nw); the
   455	    g₁-parity column; the cost (rows)^{2+o(1)}; and transcript invariance (T). LV §6 also supplies
   456	    characters, exceptional square classes and complexity bounds. None of this is established at these
   457	    heights by the published theorem.
   458	  - **HECM's running-time theorem**, as in pcest. Theorem A′ replaces HECM by Pollard–Strassen, at the
   459	    constants of the table; this also needs LV6 without HECM.
   460	  - **The LV Lemma 5.1 irreducibility transfer**, at the level of statements, now with constant
   461	    coefficient ≈ Nw/M^d.
   462	  - **The internal, unrefereed hypD/lemmaM results** used by pcest's Theorem A: Theorems K, S′ and DD.
   463	- **Conclusion.** Every N is factored in expected time L_N[1/2, (1 + θ)/√2 + o(1)].
   464	- Optimizing μ gives the table. The infimum is (1 + 3/(d+1))/√2: d = 9 gives 0.9192, d = 11 gives 0.8839,
   465	  d = 19 gives 0.8132.
   466	- c < 1 holds for d = 9 and d = 11 from k = 13 on, for sufficiently small η₀.
   467	
   468	*Proof.* pcest Theorem A's proof (steps 1–5) applies verbatim to (a‴_k; μ):
   469	- Theorem 4.3(ii) is replaced by Theorem LD* + FM + Prop PZ, applied in the order of §1 (moments,
   470	  rejection, selection).

 succeeded in 0ms:
   471	- T_SQ = S²L^{o(1)} = L^{θ/(2a)+o(1)}.
   472	- The cost is max(a + 1/√2, a + θ/(2a), 2a) = (1+θ)/√2 at a = θ/√2.
   473	- Sampling w costs (log N)^{O(1)} per field. ∎
   474	
   475	## 7. Design (a″_k): what remains open
   476	
   477	**Prop 7.1 (a sufficient missing estimate for (a″_k)) [proved reduction; the estimate itself is open].**
   478	- Steps 0–3 of §5 hold for (a″_k) verbatim, with w = 1 and the old X*. Step 4 is the only step that
   479	  averages over w.
   480	- Without Step 4, the algebraic factor depends on g through the fibre index j (via r₀), not only through
   481	  n. So Step 5's decoupling is unavailable.
   482	- LD* for (a″_k) follows from this estimate:
   483	
   484	      E_ℓ Σ_{P∈𝒫_ℓ} Σ_{q≤2S²} Σ_{P′: |det(P,P′)|=ℓq} Σ_{n∈𝒩_ℓ} Σ_{j ∈ 𝒥(P,P′,n): Y_{P′}(j)=1} 𝔔₀(ℓ|n|, ℓq; c_{P}(j))
   485	          ≤ L^{o(1)}·E_ℓ Σ_{P} Σ_q Σ_{P′} Σ_{n∈𝒩_ℓ} U·𝔔(ℓ²|n|q)/φ(ℓ|n|),
   486	
   487	  where:
   488	  - 𝒥(P, P′, n) is the set of admissible fibre indices (g ∈ 𝒢, both filters);
   489	  - c_P(j) = N b^d (g₁* + jb)^{−d} (mod ℓn);
   490	  - n′(j) = n′₀ ∓ qj.
   491	- It is a correlation, along each fibre, between the smoothness of an affine sequence and the lift-L² mass
   492	  at a "Möbius progression" of d-th powers. It is sufficient, not necessary.
   493	
   494	**Prop 7.2 (what the averaging in (a″_k) gives) [proved facts; the conclusion is an assessment].**
   495	- (a) For fixed rational data (ℓ, P, P′, g), r₀ is determined; c does not move it. Averaging over g moves
   496	  r₀ and the partner indicator *together*, by (2.1) of codex's report: both depend on the same j.
   497	  - This is not a proof that no averaging argument can work (codex ldbound_2: a deterministic function of
   498	    random data can be equidistributed even after conditioning).
   499	  - It only locates the coupling.
   500	- (b) Marginally, the structured residues are harmless (codex blind, §1).
   501	  - For admissible candidates, (b, g₁) = (g₁, t) = 1. Distinct admissible fractions b/g₁ ≡ u (mod t) are
   502	    separated by ≥ t/M². So each u has O(1) representations: there are no Farey spikes.
   503	  - u ↦ Nu^d is ≤ 2d^{ω(t)}-to-1, and Σ_{n smooth} A^{ω(n)} ≤ Ψ·L^{o(1)}.
   504	  - So the marginal structured-residue bound, without the partner weight, follows from L2_fam (weighted
   505	    form, codex blind (3.13)).
   506	  - The pcest §4.3 premise "representation count ≈ K on a set of measure ≈ 1/K" holds only without
   507	    primitivity or the filter.
   508	- (c) Discarding the partner weight costs 1/ρ_r = L^{Θ(1)} in this argument. Keeping it requires Prop 7.1.
   509	  - Codex gives a model in which marginal all-residue control is exact but the partner-weighted energy is
