    67	   expected time L_N[1/2, (1 + θ(d, k))/√2 + o(1)].
    68	   - Infimum over k: c(d) = (1 + 3/(d+1))/√2.
    69	   - d = 7: 0.9723. d = 9: 0.9192. d = 11: 0.8839. d = 19: 0.8132.
    70	   - c < 1 holds exactly for odd d ≥ 7 (d = 5 gives 1.0607). At d = 7 it needs k ≥ 13; at d = 9,
    71	     k ≥ 12 (with the old 1/(4k) floor: 11 and 11).
    72	   - HECM's rigour (LPP Part III) is the same caveat as in LV and hypD (§5).
    73	
    74	Compared with hypD, the conditions for (a′_k) were FM (outline) + PC_rat (open) + PC_alg (open) +
    75	LV §6. **They are now LD + LV §6.**
    76	
    77	**Experiments (pre-registered E1, toy, exact).** Setup: 8 instances at 56–64 bits, d = 3, and 9 600
    78	(field, ℓ) cells per design.
    79	- PC_rat(2D) = 1.007–1.013 (P1 holds).
    80	- PC(2D) = 1.06–1.28 (P2 holds).
    81	- |PC_rat(2D) − PC_rat(1D)| ≤ 0.003 (P3 holds).
