   317	- (i) The g with G_g(P) = ℓn lie on a line with direction (a, b) and point spacing |P|₂ ≥ V/2. The
   318	  square has chords of length ≤ M/√2. So |𝒢_P(n)| ≤ √2M/V + 1 for every n.
   319	- (ii) Consider the continuous model (g₀, g₁) uniform on [M/2, M]².
   320	  - G = g₁a − g₀b is a sum of independent uniforms on intervals of lengths |a|M/2 and bM/2.
   321	  - Its density is ≥ 1/(MV′) on a central interval of length ≥ MV′/2 ≥ MV/4.
   322	  - Removing |G| < MV/32 leaves an interval I*_P of G-values, of length ≥ MV/16, on which
   323	    |G| ∈ [MV/32, 2MV] and G has constant sign.
   324	  - For t ∈ I*_P the chord {G = t} has length ≥ (M²/4)|P|₂/(MV′) ≥ M/4, so it carries ≥ M/(8V)
   325	    lattice points for large N.
   326	  - Put I_P := I*_P/ℓ, a set of n-values of length ≥ MV/(16ℓ).
   327	- (iii) **Coprimality.** The integer points of the line g = g* + j(a, b) on which e | gcd(g₀, g₁) form
   328	  one residue class of j mod e if e | ℓn, and none otherwise, because gcd(a, b) = 1. By Möbius
   329	  inversion, for n ∈ I_P,
   330	    |𝒢_P(n)| ≥ (φ(ℓn)/ℓn)·M/(8V) − 2^{ω(ℓn)} ≥ M/(C V log log N),
