   334	t := |G(P)| = ℓ|n| and r := F̂_g(P) mod t.
   335	- (a) **(r, t) = 1, so the moving residue is reduced (item 3).**
   336	  - gcd(G, b) = gcd(g₁, b), and g₁a ≡ ℓn (mod b). Since b is a prime > B ≥ P⁺(n) and b ≠ ℓ (b ≤ V < ℓ),
   337	    gcd(g₁, b) = 1.
   338	  - gcd(G, g₁) = gcd(g₀b, g₁) = 1.
   339	  - Lemma 1.2 then gives gcd(r, t) = gcd(N, t) = 1, by preprocessing and ℓ ∤ N.
   340	  - The residue r moves with g and b. It enters only through max_r below.
   341	- (b) **Kernel and ϑ (LV 5.13, 5.18; item 4).**
