   361	  - **Sign correction (codex pcest_2).** If G and F̂ have opposite signs, the progression can cross 0;
   362	    its far endpoint then has absolute value ty − |F̂|, not ty. In every case, all terms except at most
   363	    2(|F̂|/t + 1) of them have one sign and absolute value in (|F̂|, ty − |F̂|]. This interval contains
   364	    (ty/4, ty/2], because |F̂| ≤ ty/4.
   365	  - Let X_F^max := C_d MH V_max^d with V_max := ⌊√(2Y)·S⌋, so it is common to all ℓ ∈ J. Let
   366	    𝒳 := {X_F^max ω^{−2}(1 + 1/2)^i} ∩ [X_F^max ω^{−2}, 16dX_F^max].
   367	    - 𝒳 has O(log ω) = O(Λ) elements.
   368	    - It is independent of t, P, ℓ and the residue.
   369	    - It contains a point x₁ ∈ (ty/4, ty/2]. Consecutive points differ by the factor 3/2 < 2, and
   370	      ty/4 ≥ tY_ω/4 ≥ X_F^max ω^{−2} for large N, since tY_ω ≥ X_F^max/(C_d 2^{2d}ω).
   371	  - Call t **good** if, for all x ∈ 𝒳 and all reduced residues r′,
   372	    |Ψ(x, B; t, r′) − Ψ_t(x, B)/φ(t)| ≤ Ψ_t(x, B)/(2φ(t)).
