   374	      #{smooth terms} ≥ Ψ(x₁; t, ±r) − Ψ(|F̂|; t, ±r) − 2(|F̂|/t + 1)
   375	                      ≥ Ψ(x₁)/(4t) − 3(|F̂|/t + 1) ≥ Ψ(ty)/(16t) − 3(|F̂|/t + 1).
   376	      (The progression contains every integer ≡ ±r (mod t) with absolute value in (|F̂|, x₁].)
   377	  - Dividing by y + 1 and using ϱ(ty) ≥ ϱ(16dX_F^max)/2 ≥ ρ_F/(log)^{O(1)} (by (Hi) and (C8.16)) gives
   378	    Pr ≥ ρ_F/(log)^{O(1)} − O(ωV/H). The error term is polynomially small, since |F̂|/(tY_ω) ≪ ωV/H.
   379	- Combining (b)–(d): **if t is good, then Pr_c[F_A(P) ∈ 𝒮_B] ≥ ρ_F/(log)^{O(1)} − 8d²V/H − 4/ω ≥
   380	  ρ_F/(log)^{O(1)}.**
