\]
Also
\[
\frac{\rho_F}{\rho_r}
=L^{-[h+(d+1)\nu]/(2a)+o(1)},
\]
so the prescribed S satisfies its density requirement.

For **Lemma 1.3**, primitivity of g keeps the special-q lattice at index ℓ. If ℓ divides \(g_1\), the lattice forces ℓ to divide b and therefore contains no candidate, since \(b<\ell\). Nothing uses μ = s.

