| (B), squared-denominator term | \(N^{-h-(d+1)\nu}L^{O(1)}\) |
| (C), interval-length term | \(N^{-2\nu}L^{O(1)}\) |
| (C), squared-denominator term | \(N^{(5-d)\nu-h}L^{O(1)}\) |

The last margin satisfies
\[
h+(d-5)\nu\ge(d-3)\nu+\eta_0>0,
\]
including d = 3. The principal term, non-reduced classes, negative values, denominator partition and unique-special-prime multiplicity are handled correctly.

For **LD*, Steps 0–7**:

| Step | Verdict |
|---|---|
| 0 | **CORRECT:** raw product law; ℓ-divisors of N excluded. |
| 1 | **CORRECT:** Kern is uniform in the translated offset. |
| 2 | **CORRECT:** primitivity makes κ a unit, giving the required permutation and AM–GM bound. |
| 3 | **CORRECT:** injectivity, either sign of G, and the common envelope are valid. |
| 4 | **CORRECT:** after the Lemma W repair below; no joint residue law is required. |
| 5 | **CORRECT:** the algebraic factor depends only on n; partner smoothness is bounded along a progression of step ±q. The necessary \(M/V\) margin survives. |
